# RTS performance budgets (1–7 FPS traps)

High-volume hex strategy on a **single main thread**. Never reintroduce these patterns.

## 1. Full-board spatial reset

- **Don't:** Clear/rebuild `HiddenByCell` / `SectorNodesByCell` or `FindObjectsByType` inside movement/reveal loops.
- **Do:** Boot-time `ApplyHiddenState()` in `PrologueResourceFog`. Mid-game = O(1) reads or local hex neighbors. No dynamic `InvalidateSpatialIndex()`.

## 2. TextMeshPro canvas storms

- **Don't:** Raw Unicode missing from LiberationSans SDF (`◀` `▶` `✓` `∞`) → `OnPreRenderCanvas` every frame.
- **Do:** `PrologueUiText.SanitizeForTmp()`. ASCII substitutes. `PrologueHUD.Refresh` throttled (`HudRefreshMinInterval = 0.33f`).

## 3. Synchronous survey / trail visuals

- **Don't:** Light entire path batches or full texture commits on one confirm frame.
- **Do:** Spread over **2–3 frames**; cap **5–10 cells/frame**. `PrologueSurveyMission`, `ProloguePathGroundOverlay` — `ApplyImmediate()` on confirm/drag-end, not full-board redraw.

## 4. Unbounded time-lapse / construction loops

- **Don't:** `TickAllFromTimeLapse` / week catch-up without per-frame caps while builds idle.
- **Do:** `safetyCounter > 50` → break; defer to next frame. `PrologueTimeLapse`, `PrologueConstruction`.

## Related in code

- Hand rebuild: diff before `RebuildPrologueHand`; no `RefreshHandUnlocks` feedback loops (`PrologueController`, `CardDeckController`).
- Haul / aquifer ice scans: **placement + completion only**, not every tick.

